# Downloaded corpora and everything unpacked from them. ~50 MB, re-fetchable
# with `python -m src.download`; the URLs and SHA-256 sums are recorded in
# data/raw/MANIFEST.csv, which is itself not committed since it is generated.
data/raw/

# Parsed message bodies and headers. These are real emails from 2002-2006: live
# addresses, real names and full Received: chains. The corpora are already public
# at Apache and monkey.org, but committing a parsed copy here would create a new,
# search-indexable republication of other people's correspondence under my name,
# which is a different act from citing the archive. Excluded deliberately.
#
# Reproducibility is unaffected: `python -m src.download` then the parse step
# rebuilds both files from the original sources. The derived artifacts that the
# evaluation actually consumes - features.csv.gz (numeric features only) and
# groups.csv (ids and cluster labels) - are committed, and neither contains a
# message body or an email address.
data/processed/emails.jsonl.gz
data/processed/spam_probe.jsonl.gz

